<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23624" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ŏdōrus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Without smell</i>, <i>inodorous</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ossa,</span>”
				<i>unperfumed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					6, 35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 143, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Without the sense of smell</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animalia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 7,
					6</span></i>
			 (also ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 129, 11</span></i>). </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
